Grand Chiffre de 1691 numerical correspondence data
Source: Emile Burgaud and Etienne Bazeries, Le Masque de fer (Paris, 1893),
second deciphering table, printed pp. 280-289; Gallica bpt6k1523532j f305-f314.
https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k1523532j
Public-domain historical numerical correspondences; scans are not distributed.
The ASCII transcription was cross-checked with Daniel Bourdeau's transcription:
https://github.com/dbourdeau/cyphersolver/blob/main/targets/feuquieres/grand_chiffre_1691.tsv
Git blob 45156e42dcda980c0f7bc1c6fc594c2328980ec3 (retrieved 2026-10-31).
Attribution: Daniel Bourdeau, Unsolved Historical Ciphers, September 2026.
https://dbourdeau.github.io/cyphersolver/catinat1691.html (CC BY 4.0 text).
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Cube changes verified against primary scans: group 502 reads Bien in f312
(replacing Rien); alternative capitalization at 164 (Ie-Je, f307) and 215
(Iu-Ju, f308) follows the printed deciphering table. Accents are omitted explicitly; blanks, nulls, cancellation,
printed alternatives and Geneve? are distinguished. No inference fills blanks.
No modern solver code, dictionary, scan or historical message is bundled.

Bellaso 1553 numerical profile facts
Source: Giovan Battista Bellaso, La cifra (Venice, 1553), ordinary continuous
countersign instructions/example and fixed eleven-pair table, book pp.[3-5].
BEIC digital library, IE2960948; PDF FL2960976, pp.6-8 including library cover.
https://preserver.beic.it/delivery/DeliveryManagerServlet?dps_pid=IE2960948
Cross-check: https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bellaso_1553.JPG
Public-domain numerical correspondences independently implemented as rotations.
Canonical capitals transcribe printed u/V as V and long s as S; the example
begins Sybouey. No 1555/1564 variant, line-verse schedule or in-band y separator
is inferred. The BEIC PDF attributes its facsimile to BEIC under CC BY 4.0;
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ . No scan, PDF, article or modern
solver implementation is distributed with Cube.

ROT8000 numerical profile facts
Specification: rottytooth/rot8000 revision c47905631615173e51ac88e0901c4be642a1c8aa.
Cube independently implements the fixed ranges and half-cycle using range
arithmetic. No upstream GPL implementation or generated mapping table is bundled.

ACA table and conjugated fractionation numerical profile facts
Sources: American Cryptogram Association Cadenus, Swagman, Nihilist
Transposition and CM Bifid specification sheets, reviewed 2026-11-01:
https://www.cryptogram.org/downloads/aca.info/ciphers/Cadenus.pdf
https://www.cryptogram.org/downloads/aca.info/ciphers/Swagman.pdf
https://www.cryptogram.org/downloads/aca.info/ciphers/NihilistTransposition.pdf
https://www.cryptogram.org/downloads/aca.info/ciphers/CMBifid.pdf
Independent Rust implementations of the mathematical schedules; source-known
answers and numeric table facts are transcribed for verification. Cadenus
retains its fixed25rows with an explicitly bounded keyword-width extension.
No ACA document, font, scan, third-party implementation or solver is bundled.

Ubchi mathematical profile facts
Source: LANAKI, Lecture24,20March1997,revision0,pp1-2:
https://www.cryptogram.org/downloads/LANAKI%20Crypto%20Lessons/LESSON24.pdf
Original wrapper around Core's incomplete Columnar passes; the caller supplies
exact between-pass nulls by actual key-phrase word count. Numerical known-answer
facts only; no lecture/PDF, copied implementation or new dependency is bundled.

VIC English2010 mathematical profile facts
Source: the[rain]complex, VIC cipher,31May2010, original complete English example:
https://raincomplex.net/writing/title/vic-cipher/
Structural cross-check: David Kahn, Number One From Moscow, Studies in
Intelligence,1961; CIA historical release22September1993:
https://www.cia.gov/resources/csi/static/Number-One-From-Moscow.pdf
Independent key derivation and disrupted routing reuse Core's checkerboard and
column permutations. Fixed literal English alphabet, five-row schedule, supplied
split/pad/indicator evidence; no numeral/Cyrillic or later six-row variant claimed.
The source's canonical20-letter phrase prefix and numerical intermediate facts
verify the algorithm. No article, scan, full lyric, external solver or backend
code is distributed. No new library, proprietary asset or backend is required.

