the facsimile identified by the source index as a 1997 republication:
https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Grammaire_du_Solresol.pdf
Source provenance and public-domain record:
https://fr.wikisource.org/wiki/Fichier:Grammaire_du_Solresol.pdf
PDF SHA-256: c5dda1a678112e54c2de790fe3b7612ba18fef6483ee43d42f8b6f74699d6a34
Cube independently transcribes the complete seven-monosyllable French table,
all seventeen glosses and seven explicit abbreviations. No scan, font, score
or modern English translation is distributed. The finite versioned profile
retains synonyms and source distinctions; it is not a general language translator.

Symbolic alphabet source descriptions
====================================

The Tic-Tac-Toe single-grid and quarter-hour clock profiles independently
implement the published descriptions at https://www.dcode.fr/tic-tac-toe-cipher
and https://www.dcode.fr/clock-cipher, retrieved 2026-11-01. dCode.fr permits reuse
of this page content under its stated Creative Commons Attribution (CC-BY)
terms. Cube's geometry tokens, strict segmentation and validation are independent
adaptations; dCode software, images and services are not included. Full source
identity and effective definition hashes accompany operation results.

Pigpen/Rosicrucian paired-cell correspondence is independently transcribed from
Haverhill Family History Group's Pigpen Code worksheet, page1. Templars glyph
correspondence is independently transcribed from Bothwell-Gosse/Dickinson,
The Knights Templars, pp89-90, reproduced by the Grand Lodge of British Columbia
and Yukon. Betamaze correspondence and permitted geometric transformations are
independently transcribed from Terrana Cliff's alphabet, reproduced in Conlangs
DE-Cal, Spring2006, printed p289 (PDF p111). NR Tech Studio's independently
published four-feature Birds on a Wire correspondence is implemented as that
publisher's specific variant, with its B01-B26 code aliases. No source artwork,
fonts, maze puzzles, SVG renderer or third-party implementation is included.
